    "id": 4,
    "title": "The dragons’ lair",
    "summary": "Erly Alexandrino da Silva Neto from Vitória, Brazil",
    "content": "Erly Alexandrino da Silva Neto from Vitória, Brazil\n\nNGC 6188 gets its nickname — The Fighting Dragons of Ara — for the ridges of dust that appear at the center of this frame, arched against a blue backdrop of gas and dust lit by the hot young stars of open cluster NGC 6193. Below it lies the Dragon’s Egg Nebula (NGC 6164/5), a bipolar shell of gas ejected by the massive, magnetic binary star HD 148937. The imager combined 8⅔ hours of exposure taken with a 1.2-inch f/4.5 astrograph taken with Hα/OIII and OIII/SII dual-band filters and processed in the Hubble palette.\n\nAstronomy leads the astronomy hobby as the most popular magazine of its kind in the world. Get information about subscriptions, digital editions, renewals, advertising and much, much more.",
