    "id": 172,
    "title": "Watch the total solar eclipse online Aug. 12 with these free livestreams",
    "summary": "Comprehensive scientific analysis and dispatch reporting on Watch the total solar eclipse online Aug. 12 with these free livestreams.",
    "content": "Eclipses Solar Eclipses Watch the total solar eclipse online Aug. 12 with these free livestreams News By Anthony Wood Published 11 August 2026 Here's how to watch the Aug. 12 total solar eclipse live online for free.\n\nClick for next article Jump To: NASA Time and Date The European Space Agency Royal Observatory Greenwich The Virtual Telescope Project Copy link Facebook X Whatsapp Reddit Pinterest Flipboard Email Share this article 0 Join the conversation Follow us Add us as a preferred source on Google Newsletter Subscribe to our newsletter LIVE: Total Solar Eclipse 2026 | Views from Around the Globe - YouTube Watch On The Aug. 12 total solar eclipse is just one day away! Here's how you can watch the entire show live online from the comfort of your home\n\nMillions of people across Spain, Iceland and Greenland will see the moon completely hide the sun during the climactic phase of totality on Aug. 12. Countless more skywatchers across Europe will witness a deep partial solar eclipse, as the moon's curved silhouette covers a swathe of the sun's surface, while failing to cover it entirely.\n\nThankfully, we live in modern times. So there's no need for you to miss out on the solar spectacle if you find yourself outside of the path of totality, or if clouds conspire to ruin your view. Here's where to watch every phase of the 2026 total solar eclipse live online.\n\nNASA will be hosting its own livestream of the event starting at 1:15 p.m. EDT on Aug. 12, featuring live views of totality from cameras spread throughout the path of the eclipse. The visuals will be accompanied by information on the science of the incredible event and details on how the agency is working to learn more about our sun.\n\nThe NASA coverage will be hosted here on Space.com, but can also be streamed through YouTube, Twitch, NASA+, Facebook, Instagram and Amazon Prime.\n\nWatch On Time and DateTime and Date's YouTube livestream kicks off at 12 p.m. EDT (1700 GMT) on Aug. 12, bringing live views of the eclipse from Leon in northwestern Spain and the island of Mallorca, along with live commentary from journalist Anne Buckle and astrophysicist Graham Jones.\n\nWatch On The European Space AgencyAn official European Space Agency (ESA) livestream will begin at 1:30 p.m. EDT (1730 GMT) on Aug. 12. The stream will feature expert commentary on the science of the eclipse along with live views from telescopes at the Observatorio Astrofisco de Javalambre, which is located close to the Spanish city of Teruel directly in the path of totality.\n\nWatch On Royal Observatory Greenwich London's historic Royal Observatory Greenwich will host two simultaneous YouTube streams featuring live views of the partial solar eclipse starting at 1:15 p.m EDT (1815 GMT) on Aug. 12. The first livestream will be presented by Royal Observatory astronomer Greg Brown, who will discuss the science of the sun while providing expert commentary on the eclipse, while the second will offer a silent livestream, featuring visuals of the eclipse with no accompanying audio.\n\nWatch On The Virtual Telescope ProjectThe Virtual Telescope Project livestream begins at 1:20 p.m. EDT (1720 GMT) on Aug. 12, bringing real-time views from the organization's robotic telescopes in Manciano, Italy, where a partial eclipse will be visible and from the path of totality in Spain. The Virtual Telescope Project will host a separate livestream a few hours later featuring views of the Perseid meteor shower peak, which occurs overnight on Aug. 12-13.\n\nWatch On Be sure to check out our live blog for all of the latest news on the Aug. 12 total solar eclipse. We'll also have reports from Skywatching Writer Anthony Wood as he watches the eclipse unfold low in the horizon in central Spain, and also from Skywatching Editor Daisy Dobrijevic as she witnesses the spectacle during a voyage with HX Expeditions to Greenland!",
    "url": "https://www.space.com/stargazing/solar-eclipses/watch-the-total-solar-eclipse-online-aug-12-with-these-free-livestreams",
    "sourceName": "Space.com",
