    "id": 64,
    "title": "Characterization of Rocky Exoplanet Atmospheres from Ly\n                    <i>α</i>\n                    Transit Observations",
    "abstract": "Abstract\n                  \n                    Ly\n                    α\n                    transit observations are a powerful tool for probing hydrogen escape from exoplanets, but to date all Ly\n                    α\n                    transits of rocky exoplanets have yielded nondetections. Here we model the Ly\n                    α\n                    transits of rocky exoplanets across both hydrodynamic and Jeans escape regimes, varying parameters such as planet mass, temperature, hydrogen mixing ratio, and stellar distance. We find that hydrodynamic escape generally produces the largest signals, while Jeans escape can generate large signals when both hydrogen abundance and exobase temperature are high. The hydrogen mixing ratio at the homopause is the dominant factor shaping the transit depth. We evaluate the detectability of Ly\n                    α\n                    on rocky planets with current and future UV observatories, finding that existing space telescopes can only detect the deepest transits. However, future telescopes will be able to detect even shallow transits from hydrogen-poor planets. Ultimately, we find that Ly\n                    α\n                    transits can meaningfully constrain the atmospheric composition of rocky exoplanets, particularly when combined with advanced technology and multiwavelength observations.",
